---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalContact from '../components/LegalContact.astro';

// WORKING BUSINESS DRAFT — NOT A SUBSTITUTE FOR LEGAL REVIEW.
// Have this reviewed by a US-licensed attorney before relying on it
// commercially. Deliberately generic on price/timeline: BUXENA has not
// published fixed delivery charges or guaranteed lead times.
const sections = [
  { id: 'overview', title: 'Overview' },
  { id: 'quotations', title: 'Delivery Quotations and Charges' },
  { id: 'lead-times', title: 'Estimated Lead Times' },
  { id: 'freight', title: 'Freight and Curbside Delivery' },
  { id: 'access', title: 'Customer Availability and Site Access' },
  { id: 'unloading', title: 'Unloading Responsibilities' },
  { id: 'inspection', title: 'Inspection Upon Delivery' },
  { id: 'damaged', title: 'Damaged or Missing Items' },
  { id: 'redelivery', title: 'Failed Delivery and Redelivery' },
  { id: 'installation', title: 'Installation Is a Separate Service' },
  { id: 'changes', title: 'Changes to This Policy' },
  { id: 'contact', title: 'Contact Us' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Shipping & Delivery"
  description="How BUXENA quotes, arranges and delivers sauna orders across the United States."
>
  <section class="band band--tight page-head">
    <div class="shell legal">
      <span class="eyebrow">Shipping &amp; Delivery</span>
      <h1 class="display measure--tight">Shipping &amp; Delivery Policy</h1>
      <p class="legal__updated">Last Updated: July 2026</p>
      <p class="lead measure">
        This policy explains how BUXENA quotes, arranges and delivers orders.
        Because saunas are large, and every property is different, delivery
        is quoted and scheduled individually rather than at a fixed rate.
      </p>
      <LegalContact />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="shell legal">
      <nav class="legal__toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
        <ol>
          {sections.map((s, i) => (
            <li><a href={`#${s.id}`}>{i + 1}. {s.title}</a></li>
          ))}
        </ol>
      </nav>

      <div class="legal__body">
        <article id="overview">
          <h2>1. Overview</h2>
          <p>
            Most BUXENA products are large and ship by freight rather than
            standard parcel carrier. This policy covers how delivery is
            quoted, what to expect on delivery day, and what to do if
            something arrives damaged or incomplete. It should be read
            alongside our <a href="/terms/">Terms &amp; Conditions</a>.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="quotations">
          <h2>2. Delivery Quotations and Charges</h2>
          <p>
            Delivery charges depend on the product, your destination, order
            size, and site access conditions — including things like
            distance from the curb, stairs, gates, or narrow access. We do
            not publish a fixed delivery price for this reason. Your written
            quote or order confirmation will set out the delivery charge
            that applies to your specific order before you are asked to pay
            it.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="lead-times">
          <h2>3. Estimated Lead Times</h2>
          <p>
            Any lead time we give you — at quote stage or after your order
            is placed — is our best current estimate based on information
            from the manufacturer or freight carrier. Lead times can change
            due to production schedules, customs, weather, or carrier
            capacity, and should not be treated as guaranteed unless we
            confirm a specific date with you in writing. If a delay becomes
            significant, we will let you know and discuss your options.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="freight">
          <h2>4. Freight and Curbside Delivery</h2>
          <p>
            Many orders are delivered freight or curbside, meaning the
            carrier delivers to the nearest accessible point at your
            address rather than into your yard, basement, or a specific
            room. Whether a more involved delivery service is available,
            and at what cost, depends on the product, the carrier, and your
            location — ask us before ordering if you need more than
            curbside delivery.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="access">
          <h2>5. Customer Availability and Site Access</h2>
          <p>
            You are responsible for providing accurate delivery and site
            information, and for being available (or arranging someone to
            be available) to receive the delivery at the scheduled time.
            Please tell us in advance about anything that could affect
            access — steps, slopes, narrow gates, low branches, or shared
            driveways — since it can affect the delivery method or cost.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="unloading">
          <h2>6. Unloading Responsibilities</h2>
          <p>
            Unless we have expressly agreed otherwise in writing, unloading
            the shipment from the delivery vehicle and moving it to its
            final position is the customer's responsibility once the
            product has been placed at the delivery point. Some carriers
            offer liftgate or additional-labor services at extra cost —
            ask us if you think you will need one.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="inspection">
          <h2>7. Inspection Upon Delivery</h2>
          <p>
            Please inspect your shipment as soon as reasonably possible,
            ideally at the time of delivery and before signing the
            carrier's paperwork. Note any visible damage or shortage
            directly on the delivery documents where you can, take
            photographs, and let us know promptly — see Section 8.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="damaged">
          <h2>8. Damaged or Missing Items</h2>
          <p>
            If your order arrives with visible damage, or something is
            missing, contact us at{' '}
            <a href="mailto:info@buxena.com">info@buxena.com</a> as soon as
            reasonably possible with a description and photographs. Concealed
            damage that only becomes apparent once you unpack or open the
            crate should also be reported promptly, since carrier claims
            windows are time-limited. We will work with you, the carrier and
            the manufacturer toward an appropriate resolution.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="redelivery">
          <h2>9. Failed Delivery and Redelivery</h2>
          <p>
            If a delivery attempt fails because nobody was available, the
            address or access information provided was inaccurate, or the
            site was not ready to receive the shipment, additional freight
            or redelivery costs may apply. We will let you know before any
            such cost is charged.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="installation">
          <h2>10. Installation Is a Separate Service</h2>
          <p>
            Delivery and installation are separate. Installation is not
            automatically included with every purchase, and is only part of
            your order if we have expressly agreed to it in writing and it
            is reflected in your quote. See our{' '}
            <a href="/terms/">Terms &amp; Conditions</a> for more on
            installation, electrical work, and site preparation.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="changes">
          <h2>11. Changes to This Policy</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy from time to time. We will revise the
            "Last Updated" date above whenever we make a material change.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article id="contact">
          <h2>12. Contact Us</h2>
          <p>For a delivery quotation or a question about a scheduled delivery, contact:</p>
          <LegalContact />
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

